1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,240
Level one, the recruit.

2
00:00:02,720 --> 00:00:07,360
You step off a train in the south of

3
00:00:04,240 --> 00:00:09,560
France. The town is called Aubagne. You

4
00:00:07,360 --> 00:00:11,720
carry one small bag with almost nothing

5
00:00:09,560 --> 00:00:14,360
in it. You left your old life in another

6
00:00:11,720 --> 00:00:15,440
country. You do not tell anyone why you

7
00:00:14,360 --> 00:00:17,360
came.

8
00:00:15,440 --> 00:00:19,000
Nobody here asks you.

9
00:00:17,360 --> 00:00:21,400
That is the first lesson this place

10
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:23,800
teaches. The Legion does not care who

11
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:25,640
you were. It cares only who you are

12
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:28,440
willing to become.

13
00:00:25,640 --> 00:00:29,960
You are 22 years old. You do not speak a

14
00:00:28,440 --> 00:00:31,360
word of French.

15
00:00:29,960 --> 00:00:34,240
You speak the language of wherever you

16
00:00:31,360 --> 00:00:36,440
were born. That is all you have.

17
00:00:34,240 --> 00:00:39,200
There are men here from 40 countries.

18
00:00:36,440 --> 00:00:40,360
Romanians, Brazilians, Nepalese,

19
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:42,680
Russians.

20
00:00:40,360 --> 00:00:44,680
Men you cannot place on a map.

21
00:00:42,680 --> 00:00:46,800
Some are running from poverty. Some are

22
00:00:44,680 --> 00:00:48,520
running from prison. Some are running

23
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:50,160
from themselves.

24
00:00:48,520 --> 00:00:51,080
You stand in a courtyard with a hundred

25
00:00:50,160 --> 00:00:53,360
others.

26
00:00:51,080 --> 00:00:55,720
Most of you cannot speak to each other.

27
00:00:53,360 --> 00:00:58,440
A sergeant searches your bag. He takes

28
00:00:55,720 --> 00:01:01,200
your phone. He takes your passport. He

29
00:00:58,440 --> 00:01:03,320
hands you a red and green tracksuit. He

30
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:05,760
gives you a bunk and a number.

31
00:01:03,320 --> 00:01:07,240
For 3 weeks, you are not a person. You

32
00:01:05,760 --> 00:01:09,720
are a candidate.

33
00:01:07,240 --> 00:01:11,360
They call this part the selection.

34
00:01:09,720 --> 00:01:12,560
It is built to find the men who will

35
00:01:11,360 --> 00:01:15,240
break.

36
00:01:12,560 --> 00:01:16,920
You run until you vomit on the gravel.

37
00:01:15,240 --> 00:01:19,560
You do pull-ups until your arms give

38
00:01:16,920 --> 00:01:20,920
out. You carry sandbags up steep hills

39
00:01:19,560 --> 00:01:22,920
in the heat.

40
00:01:20,920 --> 00:01:25,600
You sit through strange tests you do not

41
00:01:22,920 --> 00:01:28,720
understand. A doctor checks every inch

42
00:01:25,600 --> 00:01:31,840
of your body. Bad knees send men home.

43
00:01:28,720 --> 00:01:33,440
Bad teeth send men home. A weak heart

44
00:01:31,840 --> 00:01:35,240
sends men home.

45
00:01:33,440 --> 00:01:37,440
They interview you for hours about your

46
00:01:35,240 --> 00:01:40,080
past. They want to know if you fled a

47
00:01:37,440 --> 00:01:42,720
serious crime. Small trouble is forgiven

48
00:01:40,080 --> 00:01:44,440
here. Murder is not.

49
00:01:42,720 --> 00:01:46,760
They offer you a new name if you want

50
00:01:44,440 --> 00:01:47,920
one. This is called the declared

51
00:01:46,760 --> 00:01:50,320
identity.

52
00:01:47,920 --> 00:01:53,680
You can become someone new on paper.

53
00:01:50,320 --> 00:01:56,160
Many men take it. You take it, too.

54
00:01:53,680 --> 00:01:57,960
The man you used to be is gone now.

55
00:01:56,160 --> 00:02:00,640
Every night men disappear from the

56
00:01:57,960 --> 00:02:01,880
bunks. They fail the test or they simply

57
00:02:00,640 --> 00:02:03,280
quit.

58
00:02:01,880 --> 00:02:04,280
You watch their empty beds in the

59
00:02:03,280 --> 00:02:06,880
morning.

60
00:02:04,280 --> 00:02:09,160
You decide you will not be one of them.

61
00:02:06,880 --> 00:02:12,360
At the end, they read a list of numbers.

62
00:02:09,160 --> 00:02:14,920
Your number is on it. You have passed.

63
00:02:12,360 --> 00:02:18,920
You sign a contract for 5 years.

64
00:02:14,920 --> 00:02:21,480
You belong to France now, body and soul.

65
00:02:18,920 --> 00:02:22,680
Level two, the legionnaire.

66
00:02:21,480 --> 00:02:24,920
They send you to a base near

67
00:02:22,680 --> 00:02:27,160
Castelnaudary. It is a training base in

68
00:02:24,920 --> 00:02:29,360
the countryside. For 4 months, this

69
00:02:27,160 --> 00:02:31,360
place is your whole world. You learn to

70
00:02:29,360 --> 00:02:33,680
march in formation. You learn to shoot a

71
00:02:31,360 --> 00:02:35,160
rifle. You learn to obey before you

72
00:02:33,680 --> 00:02:36,720
understand.

73
00:02:35,160 --> 00:02:39,520
The instructors were once recruits like

74
00:02:36,720 --> 00:02:40,880
you. They scream at you in French.

75
00:02:39,520 --> 00:02:43,320
You learn the language because you have

76
00:02:40,880 --> 00:02:45,400
no choice. A man who cannot understand

77
00:02:43,320 --> 00:02:46,800
an order fails.

78
00:02:45,400 --> 00:02:48,000
You memorize the code of honor of the

79
00:02:46,800 --> 00:02:49,600
legionnaire.

80
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:50,680
Seven articles you must recite from

81
00:02:49,600 --> 00:02:53,040
memory.

82
00:02:50,680 --> 00:02:54,600
You learn the Legion's motto. The Legion

83
00:02:53,040 --> 00:02:56,959
is our homeland.

84
00:02:54,600 --> 00:02:58,880
That phrase grows heavier every year.

85
00:02:56,959 --> 00:03:00,760
You sing while you march.

86
00:02:58,880 --> 00:03:03,239
The Legion marches slower than any unit

87
00:03:00,760 --> 00:03:05,080
in France. 88 steps a minute while the

88
00:03:03,239 --> 00:03:06,880
rest march faster.

89
00:03:05,080 --> 00:03:09,200
You sing old songs about death and

90
00:03:06,880 --> 00:03:11,840
brotherhood. Your feet bleed inside your

91
00:03:09,200 --> 00:03:13,320
boots on long marches. You bandage them

92
00:03:11,840 --> 00:03:15,640
and keep walking.

93
00:03:13,320 --> 00:03:17,480
You learn to live with little sleep.

94
00:03:15,640 --> 00:03:18,959
You learn that pain is just information

95
00:03:17,480 --> 00:03:21,160
you can ignore.

96
00:03:18,959 --> 00:03:23,480
The hardest test comes near the end. It

97
00:03:21,160 --> 00:03:25,080
is the march called the Képi blanc.

98
00:03:23,480 --> 00:03:27,080
You march for days with everything on

99
00:03:25,080 --> 00:03:29,640
your back. At the finish, there is a

100
00:03:27,080 --> 00:03:31,640
ceremony at night. You stand in silent

101
00:03:29,640 --> 00:03:33,120
formation under the stars.

102
00:03:31,640 --> 00:03:35,239
For the first time, you place the white

103
00:03:33,120 --> 00:03:37,800
Képi on your head. You are no longer a

104
00:03:35,239 --> 00:03:39,320
candidate. You are a legionnaire.

105
00:03:37,800 --> 00:03:41,680
You feel something you have not felt in

106
00:03:39,320 --> 00:03:42,920
years. You belong to something larger

107
00:03:41,680 --> 00:03:44,519
than yourself.

108
00:03:42,920 --> 00:03:45,640
The men beside you feel like brothers

109
00:03:44,519 --> 00:03:47,760
already.

110
00:03:45,640 --> 00:03:50,239
They assign you to a regiment. Maybe the

111
00:03:47,760 --> 00:03:51,560
infantry, maybe the cavalry, maybe the

112
00:03:50,239 --> 00:03:53,600
engineers.

113
00:03:51,560 --> 00:03:55,960
You deploy within the year. They send

114
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:57,520
you to Mali, deep in the Sahara.

115
00:03:55,960 --> 00:03:59,840
You patrol villages where everyone

116
00:03:57,520 --> 00:04:01,640
watches, no one speaks.

117
00:03:59,840 --> 00:04:03,160
You ride in armored trucks down roads

118
00:04:01,640 --> 00:04:05,320
that hide bombs.

119
00:04:03,160 --> 00:04:08,000
The heat climbs past 50° in the little

120
00:04:05,320 --> 00:04:10,720
shade. You drink warm water and dream of

121
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:13,200
cold water. You learn to scan every pile

122
00:04:10,720 --> 00:04:15,520
of trash for wires. You learn to read

123
00:04:13,200 --> 00:04:17,000
fear in the faces of strangers.

124
00:04:15,520 --> 00:04:19,200
One afternoon, a friend steps on a

125
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:20,040
buried mine. He does not come home with

126
00:04:19,200 --> 00:04:21,680
you.

127
00:04:20,040 --> 00:04:22,840
You carry his coffin with five other

128
00:04:21,680 --> 00:04:24,680
men.

129
00:04:22,840 --> 00:04:27,240
You learn the brotherhood is real, not

130
00:04:24,680 --> 00:04:28,520
just words. You also learn exactly what

131
00:04:27,240 --> 00:04:30,800
it costs.

132
00:04:28,520 --> 00:04:33,120
You are 23 years old. You have already

133
00:04:30,800 --> 00:04:35,240
watched a man die. You are not the same

134
00:04:33,120 --> 00:04:37,840
person who stepped off that train. You

135
00:04:35,240 --> 00:04:40,480
never will be again.

136
00:04:37,840 --> 00:04:42,720
Level three, the corporal.

137
00:04:40,480 --> 00:04:44,320
You have served two full years.

138
00:04:42,720 --> 00:04:45,560
You now speak French well enough to give

139
00:04:44,320 --> 00:04:47,160
an order.

140
00:04:45,560 --> 00:04:49,040
Your sergeant puts your name forward for

141
00:04:47,160 --> 00:04:50,600
the corporal course.

142
00:04:49,040 --> 00:04:51,680
You go back to a school for several

143
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:53,960
weeks.

144
00:04:51,680 --> 00:04:55,840
You learn to lead a small team of men.

145
00:04:53,960 --> 00:04:57,640
Four or five legionnaires who will look

146
00:04:55,840 --> 00:05:00,040
to you for everything.

147
00:04:57,640 --> 00:05:01,480
You study tactics and first aid and how

148
00:05:00,040 --> 00:05:03,800
to command.

149
00:05:01,480 --> 00:05:05,000
When you pass, they sew the stripes onto

150
00:05:03,800 --> 00:05:07,200
your sleeve.

151
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:09,720
You are a caporal now.

152
00:05:07,200 --> 00:05:12,160
The very bottom rung of leadership.

153
00:05:09,720 --> 00:05:14,120
Your whole job changes overnight.

154
00:05:12,160 --> 00:05:15,240
Yesterday, you only had to keep yourself

155
00:05:14,120 --> 00:05:17,240
alive.

156
00:05:15,240 --> 00:05:18,600
Today, you are responsible for four

157
00:05:17,240 --> 00:05:20,320
other men.

158
00:05:18,600 --> 00:05:22,760
You wake them in the morning. You

159
00:05:20,320 --> 00:05:24,240
inspect their boots and their rifles.

160
00:05:22,760 --> 00:05:26,000
You teach the new arrivals what you

161
00:05:24,240 --> 00:05:27,720
learned the hard way.

162
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:28,680
They remind you of yourself two years

163
00:05:27,720 --> 00:05:31,040
ago.

164
00:05:28,680 --> 00:05:33,200
Scared, far from home,

165
00:05:31,040 --> 00:05:34,760
unable to speak the language.

166
00:05:33,200 --> 00:05:35,760
You are harder on them than you should

167
00:05:34,760 --> 00:05:38,800
be.

168
00:05:35,760 --> 00:05:41,080
That hardness is how they will survive.

169
00:05:38,800 --> 00:05:42,840
You deploy again with your team.

170
00:05:41,080 --> 00:05:44,600
This time, they send you to the jungle

171
00:05:42,840 --> 00:05:46,160
of French Guiana.

172
00:05:44,600 --> 00:05:48,240
You patrol the border against gold

173
00:05:46,160 --> 00:05:49,880
miners and smugglers.

174
00:05:48,240 --> 00:05:51,080
The jungle is a different enemy than the

175
00:05:49,880 --> 00:05:53,120
desert.

176
00:05:51,080 --> 00:05:55,160
Everything there bites you.

177
00:05:53,120 --> 00:05:56,600
Everything wants to rot your skin and

178
00:05:55,160 --> 00:05:58,400
your feet.

179
00:05:56,600 --> 00:06:00,280
You lead your men across rivers and

180
00:05:58,400 --> 00:06:02,080
through black swamps.

181
00:06:00,280 --> 00:06:03,640
You make decisions that keep other men

182
00:06:02,080 --> 00:06:06,520
alive.

183
00:06:03,640 --> 00:06:09,200
One night on patrol, you make a mistake.

184
00:06:06,520 --> 00:06:11,040
You take the wrong path in the darkness.

185
00:06:09,200 --> 00:06:12,440
Your team is lost in the jungle for

186
00:06:11,040 --> 00:06:14,720
hours.

187
00:06:12,440 --> 00:06:16,400
No one dies, but it nearly ends in

188
00:06:14,720 --> 00:06:17,880
disaster.

189
00:06:16,400 --> 00:06:19,160
Your sergeant tears into you when you

190
00:06:17,880 --> 00:06:21,919
return.

191
00:06:19,160 --> 00:06:23,520
You never make that mistake again.

192
00:06:21,919 --> 00:06:25,240
You learn that the failures belong to

193
00:06:23,520 --> 00:06:28,240
the leader alone.

194
00:06:25,240 --> 00:06:30,200
The successes belong to the team.

195
00:06:28,240 --> 00:06:31,440
On leave, you visit the town near the

196
00:06:30,200 --> 00:06:33,880
base.

197
00:06:31,440 --> 00:06:35,560
You meet a French woman named Camille.

198
00:06:33,880 --> 00:06:36,880
She works behind the counter in a small

199
00:06:35,560 --> 00:06:38,320
bakery.

200
00:06:36,880 --> 00:06:39,440
She does not care that you speak with an

201
00:06:38,320 --> 00:06:41,160
accent.

202
00:06:39,440 --> 00:06:42,600
She looks at you like a man, not a

203
00:06:41,160 --> 00:06:44,080
soldier.

204
00:06:42,600 --> 00:06:45,640
You start writing letters to her when

205
00:06:44,080 --> 00:06:47,640
you deploy.

206
00:06:45,640 --> 00:06:49,160
For the first time in years, someone is

207
00:06:47,640 --> 00:06:51,080
waiting for you.

208
00:06:49,160 --> 00:06:52,560
You begin to imagine a life beyond the

209
00:06:51,080 --> 00:06:54,160
legion.

210
00:06:52,560 --> 00:06:55,560
You write to Camille about the parrots

211
00:06:54,160 --> 00:06:57,120
and the rivers.

212
00:06:55,560 --> 00:06:58,160
You do not write about the smugglers you

213
00:06:57,120 --> 00:07:01,080
fight.

214
00:06:58,160 --> 00:07:03,120
Some of the jungle stays in the jungle.

215
00:07:01,080 --> 00:07:04,600
You learn which truths a man keeps to

216
00:07:03,120 --> 00:07:07,240
himself.

217
00:07:04,600 --> 00:07:09,880
You think she might be the one.

218
00:07:07,240 --> 00:07:12,000
You are afraid to say it out loud.

219
00:07:09,880 --> 00:07:14,560
You are 25 years old.

220
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:17,560
You are quietly building a life.

221
00:07:14,560 --> 00:07:19,680
You have a woman, a rank, and brothers

222
00:07:17,560 --> 00:07:22,000
who would die for you.

223
00:07:19,680 --> 00:07:26,080
For a man who arrived with one bag and

224
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:29,320
no name, that is everything.

225
00:07:26,080 --> 00:07:31,360
Level four, the master corporal.

226
00:07:29,320 --> 00:07:33,280
Three more years slip by.

227
00:07:31,360 --> 00:07:34,400
Your first contract ends and you sign

228
00:07:33,280 --> 00:07:36,560
again.

229
00:07:34,400 --> 00:07:38,360
This surprises no one.

230
00:07:36,560 --> 00:07:40,120
The legion is your home now.

231
00:07:38,360 --> 00:07:41,320
There is nowhere else you would rather

232
00:07:40,120 --> 00:07:43,640
be.

233
00:07:41,320 --> 00:07:45,720
They promote you to caporal chef,

234
00:07:43,640 --> 00:07:47,040
a master corporal, the rank below the

235
00:07:45,720 --> 00:07:49,440
sergeants.

236
00:07:47,040 --> 00:07:51,800
You are an experienced soldier.

237
00:07:49,440 --> 00:07:54,320
The young legionnaires call you chef.

238
00:07:51,800 --> 00:07:56,120
They go quiet when you speak.

239
00:07:54,320 --> 00:07:57,480
You marry Camille in a small ceremony

240
00:07:56,120 --> 00:07:58,960
near the base.

241
00:07:57,480 --> 00:08:00,160
A few brothers from your unit stand

242
00:07:58,960 --> 00:08:02,480
beside you.

243
00:08:00,160 --> 00:08:04,480
Your own family is not there.

244
00:08:02,480 --> 00:08:05,640
They live in another country, another

245
00:08:04,480 --> 00:08:07,800
life.

246
00:08:05,640 --> 00:08:09,720
You did not invite them.

247
00:08:07,800 --> 00:08:10,800
Camille knows only the man you became

248
00:08:09,720 --> 00:08:12,400
here.

249
00:08:10,800 --> 00:08:14,080
She does not know the boy who fled

250
00:08:12,400 --> 00:08:16,960
across a border.

251
00:08:14,080 --> 00:08:18,360
You are content to keep it that way.

252
00:08:16,960 --> 00:08:19,840
A year into the marriage, she gives

253
00:08:18,360 --> 00:08:21,760
birth to a son.

254
00:08:19,840 --> 00:08:23,080
You name him Lucas.

255
00:08:21,760 --> 00:08:24,840
You hold him in the hospital in your

256
00:08:23,080 --> 00:08:27,680
hands shake.

257
00:08:24,840 --> 00:08:29,600
You have killed men and buried friends.

258
00:08:27,680 --> 00:08:31,360
You have never been this afraid in your

259
00:08:29,600 --> 00:08:33,240
life.

260
00:08:31,360 --> 00:08:34,360
You deploy again 2 months after he is

261
00:08:33,240 --> 00:08:36,159
born.

262
00:08:34,360 --> 00:08:37,440
They send you to the Sahel.

263
00:08:36,159 --> 00:08:38,560
The fighting is worse than it was

264
00:08:37,440 --> 00:08:40,560
before.

265
00:08:38,560 --> 00:08:43,000
Your convoy's ambushed on a dirt road

266
00:08:40,560 --> 00:08:44,720
one morning. You return fire from behind

267
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:46,600
a burning truck.

268
00:08:44,720 --> 00:08:48,040
Two of your men are hit.

269
00:08:46,600 --> 00:08:49,480
You drag one of them to cover with your

270
00:08:48,040 --> 00:08:52,160
bare hands.

271
00:08:49,480 --> 00:08:54,440
He lives because of you.

272
00:08:52,160 --> 00:08:56,520
They recommend you for a citation.

273
00:08:54,440 --> 00:09:00,040
You do not feel like a hero.

274
00:08:56,520 --> 00:09:01,560
You only want to get home to your son.

275
00:09:00,040 --> 00:09:03,120
At night in the desert, you stare at a

276
00:09:01,560 --> 00:09:04,680
photo of Lucas.

277
00:09:03,120 --> 00:09:06,720
You wonder what kind of father a man

278
00:09:04,680 --> 00:09:10,440
like you can be.

279
00:09:06,720 --> 00:09:12,560
You decide you will try anyway.

280
00:09:10,440 --> 00:09:13,920
You write Camille every week.

281
00:09:12,560 --> 00:09:15,200
You tell her about the heat and the

282
00:09:13,920 --> 00:09:17,240
boredom.

283
00:09:15,200 --> 00:09:18,839
You do not tell her about the ambushes

284
00:09:17,240 --> 00:09:20,680
or the blood.

285
00:09:18,839 --> 00:09:22,080
Some things a husband keeps off the

286
00:09:20,680 --> 00:09:23,960
page.

287
00:09:22,080 --> 00:09:25,720
She writes back about Lucas and his

288
00:09:23,960 --> 00:09:27,160
first words.

289
00:09:25,720 --> 00:09:28,320
Those letters keep you alive in the

290
00:09:27,160 --> 00:09:30,040
desert.

291
00:09:28,320 --> 00:09:31,600
You understand now what you fight to

292
00:09:30,040 --> 00:09:33,800
come home to.

293
00:09:31,600 --> 00:09:35,080
It is no longer France or the legion

294
00:09:33,800 --> 00:09:37,720
alone.

295
00:09:35,080 --> 00:09:39,680
It is a small boy and a woman in a

296
00:09:37,720 --> 00:09:42,240
bakery town.

297
00:09:39,680 --> 00:09:44,680
Camille worries every time you leave.

298
00:09:42,240 --> 00:09:47,080
She never asks you to quit the Legion.

299
00:09:44,680 --> 00:09:49,160
She understands what it means to you.

300
00:09:47,080 --> 00:09:50,920
You love her more for that than she will

301
00:09:49,160 --> 00:09:53,160
ever know.

302
00:09:50,920 --> 00:09:56,480
You are 28 years old.

303
00:09:53,160 --> 00:09:57,920
You have a wife, a son, and a war to

304
00:09:56,480 --> 00:10:00,680
survive.

305
00:09:57,920 --> 00:10:03,520
You intend to survive it.

306
00:10:00,680 --> 00:10:05,120
Level five, the sergeant.

307
00:10:03,520 --> 00:10:07,440
The Legion sends you to the school for

308
00:10:05,120 --> 00:10:10,360
non-commissioned officers. This is a

309
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:12,240
real promotion, not just another stripe.

310
00:10:10,360 --> 00:10:15,800
You cross a line that most legionnaires

311
00:10:12,240 --> 00:10:17,200
never cross. You become a sous-officier,

312
00:10:15,800 --> 00:10:19,920
a sergeant.

313
00:10:17,200 --> 00:10:22,440
The course is long and brutal. You study

314
00:10:19,920 --> 00:10:23,480
tactics, navigation, leadership, and

315
00:10:22,440 --> 00:10:25,480
law.

316
00:10:23,480 --> 00:10:27,000
You learn to plan an operation, not

317
00:10:25,480 --> 00:10:28,560
merely follow one.

318
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:30,960
You learn to think two moves ahead of

319
00:10:28,560 --> 00:10:33,320
the enemy. You pass, and they pin the

320
00:10:30,960 --> 00:10:34,480
rank on your chest. You are a sergeant

321
00:10:33,320 --> 00:10:37,000
now.

322
00:10:34,480 --> 00:10:40,280
You command a section of around 30 men,

323
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:41,960
30 rifles, and 30 lives in your hands.

324
00:10:40,280 --> 00:10:44,240
You are no longer just a soldier who

325
00:10:41,960 --> 00:10:45,400
fights. You decide how the fight

326
00:10:44,240 --> 00:10:48,000
happens.

327
00:10:45,400 --> 00:10:49,400
The young corporals report to you now.

328
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:50,440
You remember being one of them in the

329
00:10:49,400 --> 00:10:52,160
jungle.

330
00:10:50,440 --> 00:10:55,520
You try to be the sergeant you wish you

331
00:10:52,160 --> 00:10:58,120
had. Hard, but fair. Honest with your

332
00:10:55,520 --> 00:10:59,760
men, even when the truth is ugly.

333
00:10:58,120 --> 00:11:02,480
You deploy to lead your section into

334
00:10:59,760 --> 00:11:04,720
real combat. This time, the mission is

335
00:11:02,480 --> 00:11:06,839
in the mountains. You plan night patrols

336
00:11:04,720 --> 00:11:09,160
and ambushes of your own. You call in

337
00:11:06,839 --> 00:11:12,280
fire support over the radio. You make

338
00:11:09,160 --> 00:11:14,400
decisions in seconds that men die by.

339
00:11:12,280 --> 00:11:17,640
One night, a young legionnaire freezes

340
00:11:14,400 --> 00:11:18,920
under fire. He is 19, and his legs will

341
00:11:17,640 --> 00:11:20,880
not move.

342
00:11:18,920 --> 00:11:23,080
You crawl across open ground to reach

343
00:11:20,880 --> 00:11:25,560
him. You talk him through it in a calm

344
00:11:23,080 --> 00:11:27,800
voice. You get him back on his feet and

345
00:11:25,560 --> 00:11:30,320
moving. He survives the deployment

346
00:11:27,800 --> 00:11:31,600
because of you. He thanks you with tears

347
00:11:30,320 --> 00:11:33,440
in his eyes.

348
00:11:31,600 --> 00:11:34,640
You think back to own first deployment

349
00:11:33,440 --> 00:11:36,120
in Mali.

350
00:11:34,640 --> 00:11:37,680
You think of the men who pushed you when

351
00:11:36,120 --> 00:11:40,720
you wanted to quit.

352
00:11:37,680 --> 00:11:43,440
Now, you are that man for someone else.

353
00:11:40,720 --> 00:11:45,760
Back home, Lucas is three now.

354
00:11:43,440 --> 00:11:47,920
He runs to the door when you come home.

355
00:11:45,760 --> 00:11:49,720
He does not understand where you go.

356
00:11:47,920 --> 00:11:51,120
He only knows that you leave and then

357
00:11:49,720 --> 00:11:52,720
come back.

358
00:11:51,120 --> 00:11:53,840
You promise him you will always come

359
00:11:52,720 --> 00:11:56,000
back.

360
00:11:53,840 --> 00:11:57,160
You know it is a promise no soldier can

361
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:59,280
keep.

362
00:11:57,160 --> 00:12:01,440
You make it anyway because he needs to

363
00:11:59,280 --> 00:12:03,280
hear it.

364
00:12:01,440 --> 00:12:04,240
Camille worries more now than she used

365
00:12:03,280 --> 00:12:05,840
to.

366
00:12:04,240 --> 00:12:07,080
Each deployment is harder on her than

367
00:12:05,840 --> 00:12:09,160
the last.

368
00:12:07,080 --> 00:12:11,560
She has new gray in her hair.

369
00:12:09,160 --> 00:12:13,240
She never asks you to leave the Legion.

370
00:12:11,560 --> 00:12:14,920
She knows it would be like asking you to

371
00:12:13,240 --> 00:12:16,840
stop breathing.

372
00:12:14,920 --> 00:12:18,640
You earn the respect of officers above

373
00:12:16,840 --> 00:12:19,920
you. They mention your name in their

374
00:12:18,640 --> 00:12:22,560
reports.

375
00:12:19,920 --> 00:12:24,480
You do not chase rank for its own sake.

376
00:12:22,560 --> 00:12:25,760
You chase it so you can protect your men

377
00:12:24,480 --> 00:12:28,840
better.

378
00:12:25,760 --> 00:12:30,160
You are 31 years old. You command 30 men

379
00:12:28,840 --> 00:12:32,520
in battle.

380
00:12:30,160 --> 00:12:33,760
You are a leader now, in name and in

381
00:12:32,520 --> 00:12:35,240
fact.

382
00:12:33,760 --> 00:12:37,120
The frightened boy from the train is

383
00:12:35,240 --> 00:12:39,960
buried deep inside.

384
00:12:37,120 --> 00:12:42,920
Most days you cannot find him at all.

385
00:12:39,960 --> 00:12:45,480
Level six, the staff sergeant.

386
00:12:42,920 --> 00:12:47,480
Four more years go by. You have served

387
00:12:45,480 --> 00:12:49,800
13 years now.

388
00:12:47,480 --> 00:12:51,400
They promote you to sergeant chef, a

389
00:12:49,800 --> 00:12:53,800
staff sergeant.

390
00:12:51,400 --> 00:12:54,800
You are one of the most experienced NCOs

391
00:12:53,800 --> 00:12:56,600
here.

392
00:12:54,800 --> 00:12:58,000
The captain asks your opinion before he

393
00:12:56,600 --> 00:12:59,360
decides.

394
00:12:58,000 --> 00:13:01,440
The young officers fresh from the

395
00:12:59,360 --> 00:13:04,640
academy lean on you.

396
00:13:01,440 --> 00:13:06,960
They have education, polish, and rank.

397
00:13:04,640 --> 00:13:08,280
You have years of war they cannot

398
00:13:06,960 --> 00:13:10,240
imagine.

399
00:13:08,280 --> 00:13:12,720
A good lieutenant knows to listen to his

400
00:13:10,240 --> 00:13:14,960
staff sergeant. A bad one learns the

401
00:13:12,720 --> 00:13:16,640
lesson the hard way.

402
00:13:14,960 --> 00:13:17,720
You become a chief instructor for part

403
00:13:16,640 --> 00:13:19,320
of the year.

404
00:13:17,720 --> 00:13:20,520
You train the new sergeants the way you

405
00:13:19,320 --> 00:13:23,200
were trained.

406
00:13:20,520 --> 00:13:25,200
You shape the next layer of leaders.

407
00:13:23,200 --> 00:13:26,880
You take quiet pride in it.

408
00:13:25,200 --> 00:13:29,200
You are building the future of the

409
00:13:26,880 --> 00:13:31,600
Legion itself.

410
00:13:29,200 --> 00:13:33,000
You deploy one final time as a field

411
00:13:31,600 --> 00:13:35,800
NCO.

412
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:38,080
This tour takes you back to West Africa.

413
00:13:35,800 --> 00:13:39,360
The enemy fights with roadside bombs and

414
00:13:38,080 --> 00:13:41,080
ambushes.

415
00:13:39,360 --> 00:13:42,280
You lose a young corporal you trained

416
00:13:41,080 --> 00:13:44,680
yourself.

417
00:13:42,280 --> 00:13:46,000
He dies on the side of a road in your

418
00:13:44,680 --> 00:13:47,840
arms.

419
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:49,320
You hold pressure on the wound, but it

420
00:13:47,840 --> 00:13:51,080
is too much.

421
00:13:49,320 --> 00:13:52,280
You write the letter to his family that

422
00:13:51,080 --> 00:13:53,840
night.

423
00:13:52,280 --> 00:13:55,200
You have written too many of these

424
00:13:53,840 --> 00:13:57,600
letters now.

425
00:13:55,200 --> 00:13:59,000
Each one takes a piece that never comes

426
00:13:57,600 --> 00:14:01,120
back.

427
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:02,120
You start to feel all the years in your

428
00:14:01,120 --> 00:14:04,440
body.

429
00:14:02,120 --> 00:14:05,680
Your knees ache from a thousand jumps

430
00:14:04,440 --> 00:14:07,880
and marches.

431
00:14:05,680 --> 00:14:09,240
Your hearing fades with every burst of

432
00:14:07,880 --> 00:14:10,640
gunfire.

433
00:14:09,240 --> 00:14:12,880
You wake at night with your heart

434
00:14:10,640 --> 00:14:15,240
pounding for no reason.

435
00:14:12,880 --> 00:14:16,680
The war follows you home and sits in the

436
00:14:15,240 --> 00:14:19,200
corner.

437
00:14:16,680 --> 00:14:21,040
Camille notices the change in you.

438
00:14:19,200 --> 00:14:22,360
She holds you when you wake up shaking

439
00:14:21,040 --> 00:14:24,320
in the dark.

440
00:14:22,360 --> 00:14:27,520
She never asks you to explain what you

441
00:14:24,320 --> 00:14:29,600
saw. She just stays.

442
00:14:27,520 --> 00:14:32,600
Lucas is seven now.

443
00:14:29,600 --> 00:14:34,240
He asks you why you have so many scars.

444
00:14:32,600 --> 00:14:35,560
You tell him you fell down a lot as a

445
00:14:34,240 --> 00:14:39,320
young man.

446
00:14:35,560 --> 00:14:41,000
He laughs at that. You do not laugh.

447
00:14:39,320 --> 00:14:42,440
You wonder how long you can keep him

448
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:43,960
from the truth.

449
00:14:42,440 --> 00:14:45,720
You consider leaving the Legion when

450
00:14:43,960 --> 00:14:48,120
this contract ends.

451
00:14:45,720 --> 00:14:49,280
You picture a quiet job and an ordinary

452
00:14:48,120 --> 00:14:51,200
life.

453
00:14:49,280 --> 00:14:52,320
Then, the captain calls you into his

454
00:14:51,200 --> 00:14:55,200
office.

455
00:14:52,320 --> 00:14:57,320
He offers something you did not expect.

456
00:14:55,200 --> 00:14:59,080
A path you thought was closed to men who

457
00:14:57,320 --> 00:15:01,440
rose from the ranks.

458
00:14:59,080 --> 00:15:04,080
You tell him you need to think about it.

459
00:15:01,440 --> 00:15:05,600
You already know your answer.

460
00:15:04,080 --> 00:15:06,680
You talk it over with Camille that

461
00:15:05,600 --> 00:15:09,640
weekend.

462
00:15:06,680 --> 00:15:11,680
She sees the hunger still in your eyes.

463
00:15:09,640 --> 00:15:14,520
She tells you to take it.

464
00:15:11,680 --> 00:15:16,000
She married a legionnaire, she says, not

465
00:15:14,520 --> 00:15:18,080
a clerk.

466
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:19,640
You love her for understanding you so

467
00:15:18,080 --> 00:15:22,240
well.

468
00:15:19,640 --> 00:15:24,680
You are 35 years old.

469
00:15:22,240 --> 00:15:26,040
You understand what this life costs a

470
00:15:24,680 --> 00:15:28,680
man.

471
00:15:26,040 --> 00:15:30,960
You are not finished yet.

472
00:15:28,680 --> 00:15:33,080
Level seven, the adjutant.

473
00:15:30,960 --> 00:15:36,160
You sign one more contract and you keep

474
00:15:33,080 --> 00:15:39,000
climbing. They promote you to adjutant.

475
00:15:36,160 --> 00:15:40,400
A warrant officer, a senior NCO with

476
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:42,560
real authority.

477
00:15:40,400 --> 00:15:43,760
You are no longer a young man. You are

478
00:15:42,560 --> 00:15:46,080
40 now.

479
00:15:43,760 --> 00:15:47,760
You have 18 years behind you.

480
00:15:46,080 --> 00:15:49,760
You are the kind of soldier the recruits

481
00:15:47,760 --> 00:15:52,240
whisper about, the man who has seen

482
00:15:49,760 --> 00:15:54,720
everything and survived. The man who

483
00:15:52,240 --> 00:15:56,440
walked out of every war alive.

484
00:15:54,720 --> 00:15:59,200
Your job is no longer to lead one

485
00:15:56,440 --> 00:16:00,760
section. You manage the senior NCOs of

486
00:15:59,200 --> 00:16:03,040
an entire company.

487
00:16:00,760 --> 00:16:05,440
You bridge the officers and the men. The

488
00:16:03,040 --> 00:16:07,000
captain commands the company on paper.

489
00:16:05,440 --> 00:16:08,080
You are the one who makes it actually

490
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:09,680
run.

491
00:16:08,080 --> 00:16:10,960
You handle discipline before it reaches

492
00:16:09,680 --> 00:16:12,480
the officers.

493
00:16:10,960 --> 00:16:14,200
A legionnaire gets drunk and breaks a

494
00:16:12,480 --> 00:16:16,960
man's nose in town.

495
00:16:14,200 --> 00:16:18,520
You deal with it quietly and firmly.

496
00:16:16,960 --> 00:16:21,080
A young soldier decides he wants to

497
00:16:18,520 --> 00:16:23,160
desert. You sit with him for 3 hours in

498
00:16:21,080 --> 00:16:25,520
the dark. You talk him back from the

499
00:16:23,160 --> 00:16:26,720
edge. You remember how close you came to

500
00:16:25,520 --> 00:16:28,480
quitting once.

501
00:16:26,720 --> 00:16:30,000
You see yourself in every recruit who

502
00:16:28,480 --> 00:16:31,280
wants to run.

503
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:32,360
They post you to headquarters for a

504
00:16:31,280 --> 00:16:34,400
stretch.

505
00:16:32,360 --> 00:16:35,880
You spend less time in the field, more

506
00:16:34,400 --> 00:16:37,160
behind a desk.

507
00:16:35,880 --> 00:16:39,880
You miss the field more than you

508
00:16:37,160 --> 00:16:41,600
expected. You also know your body cannot

509
00:16:39,880 --> 00:16:43,839
do what it once did.

510
00:16:41,600 --> 00:16:45,360
You walk with a permanent limp. Old

511
00:16:43,839 --> 00:16:46,280
injuries that never healed the right

512
00:16:45,360 --> 00:16:47,680
way.

513
00:16:46,280 --> 00:16:48,720
You take pills for the pain in your

514
00:16:47,680 --> 00:16:50,880
back.

515
00:16:48,720 --> 00:16:52,880
You hide most of this from your men.

516
00:16:50,880 --> 00:16:55,680
A warrant officer is not allowed to look

517
00:16:52,880 --> 00:16:57,240
weak. You keep the pain locked away like

518
00:16:55,680 --> 00:17:00,040
everything else.

519
00:16:57,240 --> 00:17:02,120
Lucas is 12 now. He is nearly as tall as

520
00:17:00,040 --> 00:17:03,400
his mother. He tells you he wants to

521
00:17:02,120 --> 00:17:05,240
join the army.

522
00:17:03,400 --> 00:17:06,319
The thought fills you with pride and

523
00:17:05,240 --> 00:17:07,920
dread.

524
00:17:06,319 --> 00:17:10,000
You know exactly what the army takes

525
00:17:07,920 --> 00:17:11,800
from a man. You are not sure you want

526
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:13,920
that life for your son.

527
00:17:11,800 --> 00:17:15,600
You say nothing to discourage him.

528
00:17:13,920 --> 00:17:16,640
You let him keep his dream a while

529
00:17:15,600 --> 00:17:18,600
longer.

530
00:17:16,640 --> 00:17:19,640
You remember being young and hungry for

531
00:17:18,600 --> 00:17:21,240
glory.

532
00:17:19,640 --> 00:17:22,439
You remember how little you understood

533
00:17:21,240 --> 00:17:24,199
the price.

534
00:17:22,439 --> 00:17:26,480
Camille watches your face when Lucas

535
00:17:24,199 --> 00:17:28,040
talks of soldiering. She squeezes your

536
00:17:26,480 --> 00:17:29,840
hand under the table.

537
00:17:28,040 --> 00:17:31,960
She is afraid, too.

538
00:17:29,840 --> 00:17:33,400
Neither of you says it in front of him.

539
00:17:31,960 --> 00:17:34,560
You think about what comes after the

540
00:17:33,400 --> 00:17:36,400
uniform.

541
00:17:34,560 --> 00:17:37,680
You cannot picture yourself as anything

542
00:17:36,400 --> 00:17:39,360
but a soldier.

543
00:17:37,680 --> 00:17:41,720
The Legion has been your whole identity

544
00:17:39,360 --> 00:17:42,880
for decades. You wonder who you will be

545
00:17:41,720 --> 00:17:45,080
without it.

546
00:17:42,880 --> 00:17:47,480
You are 40 years old. You have given

547
00:17:45,080 --> 00:17:50,400
half of your life to the Legion. It gave

548
00:17:47,480 --> 00:17:52,440
you a home, a name, and a country.

549
00:17:50,400 --> 00:17:53,640
It has taken a heavy toll, paid in

550
00:17:52,440 --> 00:17:55,680
pieces.

551
00:17:53,640 --> 00:17:58,280
You decide the trade was worth it.

552
00:17:55,680 --> 00:18:00,600
Most days, you believe that.

553
00:17:58,280 --> 00:18:02,400
Level eight, the officer.

554
00:18:00,600 --> 00:18:03,280
Something rare happens to a man like

555
00:18:02,400 --> 00:18:05,600
you.

556
00:18:03,280 --> 00:18:08,200
The Legion offers you a commission.

557
00:18:05,600 --> 00:18:10,760
They call it an officier de rang,

558
00:18:08,200 --> 00:18:12,440
an officer risen from the ranks.

559
00:18:10,760 --> 00:18:13,640
Most officers come from the academy at

560
00:18:12,440 --> 00:18:15,760
Saint-Cyr.

561
00:18:13,640 --> 00:18:18,880
They are young, educated, and chosen

562
00:18:15,760 --> 00:18:20,440
early. You are nothing like them.

563
00:18:18,880 --> 00:18:22,280
You earned your place in the desert and

564
00:18:20,440 --> 00:18:24,760
the jungle. You become a lieutenant

565
00:18:22,280 --> 00:18:26,680
late, behind younger officers.

566
00:18:24,760 --> 00:18:30,600
The academy officers carry university

567
00:18:26,680 --> 00:18:32,360
degrees. You carry 23 years of war.

568
00:18:30,600 --> 00:18:34,720
You command a company now.

569
00:18:32,360 --> 00:18:36,920
150 men answer to you.

570
00:18:34,720 --> 00:18:38,840
You are responsible for each of them.

571
00:18:36,920 --> 00:18:41,240
Their training, their safety, their

572
00:18:38,840 --> 00:18:42,720
lives, all of it.

573
00:18:41,240 --> 00:18:43,880
You sit in the chair the captain once

574
00:18:42,720 --> 00:18:45,400
sat in.

575
00:18:43,880 --> 00:18:47,800
You once whispered advice into that

576
00:18:45,400 --> 00:18:49,840
chair as a sergeant. Now you are the one

577
00:18:47,800 --> 00:18:51,680
who must decide alone.

578
00:18:49,840 --> 00:18:52,880
You deploy your company overseas as its

579
00:18:51,680 --> 00:18:54,760
commander.

580
00:18:52,880 --> 00:18:56,240
You plan operations from a command post

581
00:18:54,760 --> 00:18:58,680
over a map.

582
00:18:56,240 --> 00:19:01,080
You no longer kick down doors yourself.

583
00:18:58,680 --> 00:19:02,680
You send other men to do it for you.

584
00:19:01,080 --> 00:19:04,000
That is harder than going in yourself

585
00:19:02,680 --> 00:19:06,080
ever was.

586
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:07,240
When you went, only your own life was on

587
00:19:06,080 --> 00:19:08,880
the line.

588
00:19:07,240 --> 00:19:10,680
Now, you gamble with the lives of a

589
00:19:08,880 --> 00:19:13,120
hundred sons.

590
00:19:10,680 --> 00:19:14,360
You lose two men on this deployment. You

591
00:19:13,120 --> 00:19:16,640
write the letters to their families

592
00:19:14,360 --> 00:19:18,000
yourself, by hand.

593
00:19:16,640 --> 00:19:19,560
You meet those families when you bring

594
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:21,680
the bodies home.

595
00:19:19,560 --> 00:19:24,080
You look their mothers in the eyes.

596
00:19:21,680 --> 00:19:26,760
You tell them their sons died brave.

597
00:19:24,080 --> 00:19:28,320
It is true, but it does not help.

598
00:19:26,760 --> 00:19:29,800
Nothing helps a mother who has buried

599
00:19:28,320 --> 00:19:31,480
her boy.

600
00:19:29,800 --> 00:19:33,360
You think of Camille and Lucas on the

601
00:19:31,480 --> 00:19:34,840
long flight home.

602
00:19:33,360 --> 00:19:36,280
You know it could be your letter someone

603
00:19:34,840 --> 00:19:38,280
else writes.

604
00:19:36,280 --> 00:19:39,760
You hold that fear quietly, the way you

605
00:19:38,280 --> 00:19:41,200
hold everything.

606
00:19:39,760 --> 00:19:42,480
Camille is proud of you when you become

607
00:19:41,200 --> 00:19:44,080
an officer.

608
00:19:42,480 --> 00:19:45,800
She sews the new insignia onto your

609
00:19:44,080 --> 00:19:47,280
uniform herself.

610
00:19:45,800 --> 00:19:48,840
She has done this for every rank you

611
00:19:47,280 --> 00:19:50,440
have ever earned.

612
00:19:48,840 --> 00:19:53,400
Her hands are not as steady as they once

613
00:19:50,440 --> 00:19:55,040
were. You both have gray hair now.

614
00:19:53,400 --> 00:19:56,680
You realize you have grown old together

615
00:19:55,040 --> 00:19:57,960
inside this life.

616
00:19:56,680 --> 00:19:59,960
You would not have survived it without

617
00:19:57,960 --> 00:20:01,400
her. You know that as surely as you know

618
00:19:59,960 --> 00:20:03,680
anything.

619
00:20:01,400 --> 00:20:05,200
Lucas is now 16.

620
00:20:03,680 --> 00:20:07,280
He watches you pin on the officer's

621
00:20:05,200 --> 00:20:08,760
rank, eyes shining.

622
00:20:07,280 --> 00:20:10,360
He is more certain than ever that he

623
00:20:08,760 --> 00:20:12,520
will be a soldier.

624
00:20:10,360 --> 00:20:14,160
You stop trying to talk him out of it.

625
00:20:12,520 --> 00:20:16,200
You only pray he never has to write the

626
00:20:14,160 --> 00:20:18,000
letters you have written.

627
00:20:16,200 --> 00:20:19,640
The other officers respect you despite

628
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:20,880
your foreign blood.

629
00:20:19,640 --> 00:20:22,400
They have heard the stories of what you

630
00:20:20,880 --> 00:20:24,120
did in the field.

631
00:20:22,400 --> 00:20:25,440
A few of the academy men resent you

632
00:20:24,120 --> 00:20:27,640
quietly.

633
00:20:25,440 --> 00:20:29,360
You do not care about their opinions.

634
00:20:27,640 --> 00:20:30,680
You answer only to your men and your

635
00:20:29,360 --> 00:20:32,800
conscience.

636
00:20:30,680 --> 00:20:34,480
You are 45 years old.

637
00:20:32,800 --> 00:20:36,080
You have come further than any recruit

638
00:20:34,480 --> 00:20:38,240
dares dream.

639
00:20:36,080 --> 00:20:39,920
A foreign boy who spoke no French now

640
00:20:38,240 --> 00:20:41,280
commands a company.

641
00:20:39,920 --> 00:20:42,480
You have paid for every step of the

642
00:20:41,280 --> 00:20:44,320
climb.

643
00:20:42,480 --> 00:20:46,120
The receipts are written on your body

644
00:20:44,320 --> 00:20:48,600
and in your memory.

645
00:20:46,120 --> 00:20:51,080
Level nine, the commander.

646
00:20:48,600 --> 00:20:53,440
Five more years pass. You rise to the

647
00:20:51,080 --> 00:20:54,480
rank of commandant, a major in the

648
00:20:53,440 --> 00:20:56,720
legion.

649
00:20:54,480 --> 00:20:58,600
You command a battalion now. Hundreds of

650
00:20:56,720 --> 00:20:59,440
men across several companies look to

651
00:20:58,600 --> 00:21:01,960
you.

652
00:20:59,440 --> 00:21:03,760
You are 50 years old. You have served

653
00:21:01,960 --> 00:21:05,440
nearly 30 years.

654
00:21:03,760 --> 00:21:06,960
You are one of the most senior officers

655
00:21:05,440 --> 00:21:09,840
risen from the ranks.

656
00:21:06,960 --> 00:21:11,360
Generals know your name and your story.

657
00:21:09,840 --> 00:21:13,720
The recruits at Aubagne hear it like a

658
00:21:11,360 --> 00:21:16,880
legend. The foreign boy who could not

659
00:21:13,720 --> 00:21:18,480
speak French and became a commander.

660
00:21:16,880 --> 00:21:20,280
You spend your days in meetings and

661
00:21:18,480 --> 00:21:23,120
planning rooms. You decide which

662
00:21:20,280 --> 00:21:25,400
companies deploy and when. You answer to

663
00:21:23,120 --> 00:21:27,640
colonels and generals above you. You

664
00:21:25,400 --> 00:21:29,000
manage budgets, logistics, and army

665
00:21:27,640 --> 00:21:31,680
politics.

666
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:34,000
The war is far from you now, on a map

667
00:21:31,680 --> 00:21:36,400
and a screen. But you remember every

668
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:38,320
desert your boots ever crossed. You

669
00:21:36,400 --> 00:21:39,680
remember the weight of every coffin you

670
00:21:38,320 --> 00:21:41,480
ever carried.

671
00:21:39,680 --> 00:21:42,760
You visit your men before they deploy

672
00:21:41,480 --> 00:21:45,120
overseas.

673
00:21:42,760 --> 00:21:46,720
You shake every hand in the line.

674
00:21:45,120 --> 00:21:48,480
You know some of these hands you will

675
00:21:46,720 --> 00:21:50,080
never shake again.

676
00:21:48,480 --> 00:21:51,680
You carry that knowledge into every

677
00:21:50,080 --> 00:21:53,560
order you give.

678
00:21:51,680 --> 00:21:55,240
You have buried too many legionnaires to

679
00:21:53,560 --> 00:21:58,680
forget the cost.

680
00:21:55,240 --> 00:22:01,400
At home, Lucas is 18 now. He joins the

681
00:21:58,680 --> 00:22:03,240
French army against your quiet hopes.

682
00:22:01,400 --> 00:22:05,520
Not the legion, but a regular line

683
00:22:03,240 --> 00:22:08,680
regiment. You could not stop him if you

684
00:22:05,520 --> 00:22:10,920
tried. You only ask him to be careful.

685
00:22:08,680 --> 00:22:12,000
He promises, the way you once promised

686
00:22:10,920 --> 00:22:13,800
Camille.

687
00:22:12,000 --> 00:22:16,800
You understand now how empty that

688
00:22:13,800 --> 00:22:19,160
promise can be. You let him go anyway,

689
00:22:16,800 --> 00:22:21,520
because that is what fathers do.

690
00:22:19,160 --> 00:22:24,080
Camille is graying and tired, but still

691
00:22:21,520 --> 00:22:26,680
beside you. 30 years of deployments

692
00:22:24,080 --> 00:22:28,960
never broke the marriage. Somehow, the

693
00:22:26,680 --> 00:22:30,600
distance only made it stronger.

694
00:22:28,960 --> 00:22:32,280
You still do not understand how you

695
00:22:30,600 --> 00:22:34,000
earned a woman like her.

696
00:22:32,280 --> 00:22:37,480
You stopped trying to understand it long

697
00:22:34,000 --> 00:22:40,520
ago. You just hold on with both hands.

698
00:22:37,480 --> 00:22:43,120
Your body is a museum of old wounds now.

699
00:22:40,520 --> 00:22:44,720
Your back, your knees, your ears, your

700
00:22:43,120 --> 00:22:46,360
scarred hands.

701
00:22:44,720 --> 00:22:49,320
The doctors say your field days are

702
00:22:46,360 --> 00:22:51,200
over. You already knew that. A soldier

703
00:22:49,320 --> 00:22:54,320
always knows when his time in the dirt

704
00:22:51,200 --> 00:22:55,960
is done. You command from a chair now.

705
00:22:54,320 --> 00:22:57,280
You hate it and you accept it in the

706
00:22:55,960 --> 00:22:58,960
same breath.

707
00:22:57,280 --> 00:23:01,600
You think of the boy who froze under

708
00:22:58,960 --> 00:23:03,360
fire. You think of the men you saved and

709
00:23:01,600 --> 00:23:05,160
the ones you could not.

710
00:23:03,360 --> 00:23:06,480
Their faces line up in your memory like

711
00:23:05,160 --> 00:23:08,480
a roll call.

712
00:23:06,480 --> 00:23:10,640
You write to Lucas the way Camille once

713
00:23:08,480 --> 00:23:13,000
wrote to you. You tell him to keep his

714
00:23:10,640 --> 00:23:14,600
head down and his eyes open.

715
00:23:13,000 --> 00:23:16,400
You tell him the things your sergeants

716
00:23:14,600 --> 00:23:18,280
told you long ago.

717
00:23:16,400 --> 00:23:20,080
You hope they keep him alive the way

718
00:23:18,280 --> 00:23:21,880
they kept you alive.

719
00:23:20,080 --> 00:23:24,240
You wait by the phone the way Camille

720
00:23:21,880 --> 00:23:26,080
used to wait. Now you understand what

721
00:23:24,240 --> 00:23:28,400
those years cost her.

722
00:23:26,080 --> 00:23:30,960
You are 50 years old. You command

723
00:23:28,400 --> 00:23:33,320
hundreds of men and you fear most for

724
00:23:30,960 --> 00:23:36,120
one young soldier above all.

725
00:23:33,320 --> 00:23:37,800
Your own son. Somewhere out there in a

726
00:23:36,120 --> 00:23:40,200
uniform.

727
00:23:37,800 --> 00:23:41,920
Level 10, the legend.

728
00:23:40,200 --> 00:23:44,560
You make colonel.

729
00:23:41,920 --> 00:23:47,760
After 35 years, you command an entire

730
00:23:44,560 --> 00:23:50,080
legion regiment. You are 55 years old

731
00:23:47,760 --> 00:23:52,080
and your hair has gone white.

732
00:23:50,080 --> 00:23:53,800
The boy who stepped off that train is a

733
00:23:52,080 --> 00:23:56,120
stranger to you now.

734
00:23:53,800 --> 00:23:57,840
You barely remember the country you fled

735
00:23:56,120 --> 00:23:59,920
or your old name.

736
00:23:57,840 --> 00:24:02,760
The legion gave you a new name, a new

737
00:23:59,920 --> 00:24:06,480
tongue, a new life. It took the rest of

738
00:24:02,760 --> 00:24:08,040
you in exchange slowly over the years.

739
00:24:06,480 --> 00:24:10,480
You stand on a parade ground in your

740
00:24:08,040 --> 00:24:12,720
dress uniform and white kepi.

741
00:24:10,480 --> 00:24:15,680
A thousand legionnaires stand before you

742
00:24:12,720 --> 00:24:17,920
in perfect silent lines. They sing the

743
00:24:15,680 --> 00:24:19,720
slow marching songs you sang as a

744
00:24:17,920 --> 00:24:21,680
frightened young man.

745
00:24:19,720 --> 00:24:23,120
The sound moves through your chest like

746
00:24:21,680 --> 00:24:25,080
something holy.

747
00:24:23,120 --> 00:24:26,400
You feel the decades press down on you

748
00:24:25,080 --> 00:24:28,640
like a pack.

749
00:24:26,400 --> 00:24:30,880
Soon you will retire.

750
00:24:28,640 --> 00:24:32,320
The doctors insist and your worn body

751
00:24:30,880 --> 00:24:34,280
agrees with them.

752
00:24:32,320 --> 00:24:35,840
You have given everything a man can give

753
00:24:34,280 --> 00:24:37,920
to an idea.

754
00:24:35,840 --> 00:24:39,520
France made you a citizen years ago for

755
00:24:37,920 --> 00:24:41,200
the blood you spilled.

756
00:24:39,520 --> 00:24:42,800
The legion calls it being French by

757
00:24:41,200 --> 00:24:44,560
spilled blood.

758
00:24:42,800 --> 00:24:46,000
You earned your country the hardest way

759
00:24:44,560 --> 00:24:48,440
a man can.

760
00:24:46,000 --> 00:24:49,680
No one will ever say you did not belong

761
00:24:48,440 --> 00:24:52,080
here.

762
00:24:49,680 --> 00:24:53,840
Camille stands in the crowd, her hand

763
00:24:52,080 --> 00:24:55,840
pressed over her heart.

764
00:24:53,840 --> 00:24:58,240
She has aged beside you through every

765
00:24:55,840 --> 00:25:00,600
war and every silence.

766
00:24:58,240 --> 00:25:02,680
Her hair is white now, too.

767
00:25:00,600 --> 00:25:05,320
Lucas is there as well, in his own

768
00:25:02,680 --> 00:25:07,680
uniform, a soldier now.

769
00:25:05,320 --> 00:25:09,440
Three of you, bound to a country none of

770
00:25:07,680 --> 00:25:11,280
you were born into.

771
00:25:09,440 --> 00:25:13,480
You think of the men who are not here to

772
00:25:11,280 --> 00:25:16,080
see this. The friend who stepped on a

773
00:25:13,480 --> 00:25:18,080
mine in your very first year.

774
00:25:16,080 --> 00:25:19,920
The corporal who died in your arms on a

775
00:25:18,080 --> 00:25:21,560
road in Africa.

776
00:25:19,920 --> 00:25:24,360
The young soldiers whose families

777
00:25:21,560 --> 00:25:26,480
received letters in your handwriting.

778
00:25:24,360 --> 00:25:28,000
Their faces visit you in the gray hours

779
00:25:26,480 --> 00:25:30,080
before dawn.

780
00:25:28,000 --> 00:25:31,360
You will carry all of them until the day

781
00:25:30,080 --> 00:25:33,960
you die.

782
00:25:31,360 --> 00:25:36,520
That is the real weight of the kepi, the

783
00:25:33,960 --> 00:25:38,560
part recruits cannot see.

784
00:25:36,520 --> 00:25:40,600
When you retire, you move to a small

785
00:25:38,560 --> 00:25:42,720
house in the south of France.

786
00:25:40,600 --> 00:25:44,160
You grow old in the country you adopted

787
00:25:42,720 --> 00:25:46,480
and bled for.

788
00:25:44,160 --> 00:25:48,640
You keep a garden. You walk at at night

789
00:25:46,480 --> 00:25:50,800
when sleep will not come.

790
00:25:48,640 --> 00:25:52,560
Your hands still reach for a rifle that

791
00:25:50,800 --> 00:25:55,320
is no longer there.

792
00:25:52,560 --> 00:25:57,000
The war never fully leaves a man.

793
00:25:55,320 --> 00:25:58,400
You made your peace with that a long

794
00:25:57,000 --> 00:25:59,960
time ago.

795
00:25:58,400 --> 00:26:01,840
You sit on the porch in the evenings

796
00:25:59,960 --> 00:26:03,640
with Camille beside you.

797
00:26:01,840 --> 00:26:05,760
You do not speak much.

798
00:26:03,640 --> 00:26:06,800
After all these years, you do not need

799
00:26:05,760 --> 00:26:09,520
to.

800
00:26:06,800 --> 00:26:11,280
Somewhere far away right now, a train is

801
00:26:09,520 --> 00:26:13,800
pulling into Aubagne.

802
00:26:11,280 --> 00:26:15,520
A young man steps off with one bag and a

803
00:26:13,800 --> 00:26:17,840
pass to Berry.

804
00:26:15,520 --> 00:26:20,480
He does not speak a word of French.

805
00:26:17,840 --> 00:26:22,920
He does not know a single soul.

806
00:26:20,480 --> 00:26:24,320
He is afraid, though he would rather die

807
00:26:22,920 --> 00:26:26,160
than admit it.

808
00:26:24,320 --> 00:26:28,720
He has heard stories of glory and

809
00:26:26,160 --> 00:26:30,880
brotherhood and a fresh start.

810
00:26:28,720 --> 00:26:32,880
He has no idea what the Legion will

811
00:26:30,880 --> 00:26:34,720
truly ask of him.

812
00:26:32,880 --> 00:26:36,640
He does not know about the marches that

813
00:26:34,720 --> 00:26:38,440
bleed your feet raw.

814
00:26:36,640 --> 00:26:40,520
He does not know about the friends he

815
00:26:38,440 --> 00:26:42,640
will lower into the ground.

816
00:26:40,520 --> 00:26:44,440
He does not know about the man he is

817
00:26:42,640 --> 00:26:46,480
going to become.

818
00:26:44,440 --> 00:26:48,280
But he will learn all of it.

819
00:26:46,480 --> 00:26:51,120
They always do.

820
00:26:48,280 --> 00:26:53,160
He signs his name, or a new one, on a

821
00:26:51,120 --> 00:26:55,400
five-year contract.

822
00:26:53,160 --> 00:26:57,160
The white kepi waits for him at the end

823
00:26:55,400 --> 00:27:01,000
of a long road.

824
00:26:57,160 --> 00:27:01,000
And the cycle continues.

